  es: 'The most common mistake here is confusing qualities that are similar in structure: rápido and único both end in -o and both change to -a, but mean completely different things. Another trap is forgetting that fácil and verdad do not change for gender at all, unlike bonito, verdadero, rápido, único, which do change. A third trap is confusing the linking word es with soy: es is used for any thing or situation, soy only when the speaker is talking about themselves. The check is simple: first work out who or what is being talked about, then which quality is needed, and only then choose its form by gender.',
